parameters.text:
=Analyze the following extracted text from a financial report and provide a structured JSON response. Do not include any markdown formatting, preamble, or postscript. Return ONLY the raw JSON object.

Requirements:
- company: full company name
- classification: financial document type
- summary: concise, maximum 200 characters
- entities.people: list of key executives mentioned
- entities.monetary_values: financial figures mentioned. list of objects with keys label -> Description of the line item (e.g., Total net sales), value -> Amount with currency symbol
- entities.geographic_sales: list of sales per region, key -> region, value -> sales per region
- entities.financial_ratios: list of financial ratios calculated from the financial statements(e.g., Net Profit Margin, Current Ratio, Debt-to-Equity). key -> name of financial ratio, value -> percentage or ratio value
- sentiment.score: Positive, Neutral, or Negative
- sentiment.rationale: concise, maximum 200 characters
- action_items: exactly 3 concise items

Output JSON Schema:
{
  "company": "string",
  "classification": "string",
  "summary": "string",
  "entities": {
    "people": ["string"],
    "monetary_values": [
      {
        "label": "string",
        "value": "string"
      }
    ],
    "geographic_sales":[
      {
        "region": "string",
        "sales": "string"
      }
    ],
    "financial_ratios":[
      {
        "ratio": "string",
        "value": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sentiment": {
    "score": "string",
    "rationale": "string"
  },
  "action_items": ["string"]
}

Text:
{{ $json.guardrailsInput }}

parameters.jsCode:
for (const item of $input.all()) {
  const html = item.json.text;
  const filename = $('Configure').item.json['output file name'] || 'output.html';
  const buffer = Buffer.from(html, 'utf8');
  item.binary = item.binary || {};
  item.binary.data = await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(
    buffer,
    filename,
    'text/html'
  );
}
return $input.all();

const grouped = {};

for (const item of items) {
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(item.json)) {
    if (!grouped[key]) {
      grouped[key] = [];
    }
    grouped[key].push(value);
  }
}

return [{ json: grouped }];

const binaryData = await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(0, 'data');
const htmlString = binaryData.toString('utf8');

return [{
  json: {
    text: htmlString
  }
}];
